@Dengenbroker @milkroaddaily Hi, appreciate you. 
Bitcoin is underperforming and correlations still pretty high for those names. I imagine there's also the question of whether the neo's are capturing most of the value of the spot compute strength. Expect that to resolve with better lease terms over time.

What I mean is that the landlords don't get the immediate upside on improving pricing/economics for compute after a deal is locked in. Positives for them include continued shortage/appetite of compute capacity, capex plans increasing for NBIS/CRWV (need more landlords), and improving credit health of neoclouds. IMO will eventually get into landlords as the market prices in terminal value.

